## 2. Information We Process & How It Is Used

CleanMyPhone operates in accordance with strict **Data Minimization** and **Privacy-by-Design** principles. Device data is processed locally in temporary application memory (RAM) to deliver storage management utilities.

| Data Type | Purpose & Local Processing | Is Data Uploaded or Shared? |
|---|---|---|
| **Photos & Media** | Indexed locally using on-device image hashing algorithms to identify identical or duplicate photos and burst shots for user review. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **Videos & Large Files** | Analyzed locally via Android storage APIs to calculate file sizes, formats, and folders to help users reclaim storage. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **System Cache & Residual Junk** | Scanned across public/external shared storage directories to detect orphan temporary files (.tmp), application logs (.log), and hidden thumbnail caches (.thumbnails). | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **Installed Applications** | Scanned using `QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES` and `PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS` to display installed app sizes, identify space-consuming apps, and detect apps unused for 30+ days. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **System Storage & Memory Status** | Passive read-only status from system APIs (`ActivityManager`, `StatFs`) to display real-time storage and RAM utilization percentages to the user. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **Network Data Stats** | Real-time byte transfer rates measured locally via `TrafficStats` to provide network speed test diagnostics. | **No.** Never leaves your device. |
| **User Preferences** | Theme settings (dark/light mode), scan thresholds, and notification toggles stored in Android `DataStore` / `SharedPreferences`. | **No.** Stored strictly in local app sandbox. |

