## 3. Permissions & Justification

To perform core storage management and cleaning tasks, CleanMyPhone requests specific Android permissions. Each permission is strictly used for its declared user-facing feature:

### 3.1. All Files Access (`android.permission.MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE`)
- **Android Versions:** Android 11 (API level 30) and above
- **Purpose:** Required to scan, index, and allow users to delete residual junk files, empty folders, obsolete APK installers, and large files across non-media shared directories.
- **Privacy Safeguard:** Files are only modified or deleted upon explicit user confirmation in the Cleanup Basket. No files are deleted automatically in the background.

### 3.2. Read Media Permissions (`READ_MEDIA_IMAGES`, `READ_MEDIA_VIDEO`, `READ_MEDIA_AUDIO`, `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE`)
- **Android Versions:** Android 13 (API level 33)+ and legacy versions
- **Purpose:** Enables the app to generate photo thumbnails, group identical/burst photos for user review, and list large video files.
- **Privacy Safeguard:** Media files are never uploaded, backed up, or indexed off-device.

### 3.3. Query All Packages (`android.permission.QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES`) & Usage Access (`android.permission.PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS`)
- **Purpose:** Enables the App Manager to calculate storage consumption for installed applications, detect unused apps (not launched in 30+ days), and help users uninstall heavy apps.
- **Privacy Safeguard:** No application inventory, personal usage habits, or telemetry are transmitted off the device.

### 3.4. Accessibility Service API (`android.permission.BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE`)
- **Prominent Disclosure:** CleanMyPhone includes an optional, user-initiated utility to assist users in clearing app cache. Because Android OS restricts third-party apps from clearing other apps' internal cache directly, the app uses the AccessibilityService API solely to automate navigating to the system App Info settings screen and clicking "Clear Cache" for apps selected by the user.
- **Compliance & Privacy Guarantees:**
  - The Accessibility Service is **disabled by default** and requires explicit user consent and manual activation in Android Accessibility Settings.
  - The service is active **only** while an automated cache-clearing session is running.
  - It does **not** collect, store, or transmit any user information or personal data.
  - It does **not** read screen text outside system App Info settings, does not intercept passwords, does not log keystrokes, and does not alter system settings without user control.

### 3.5. Notifications (`android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS`)
- **Purpose:** Delivers local alerts, such as when deep scanning finishes or storage threshold warnings occur.
- **Privacy Safeguard:** Notifications are triggered locally and can be enabled or disabled at any time in Settings.

### 3.6. Advertising Identifier (`com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID`)
- **Purpose:** Used by Google Mobile Ads (AdMob) to display non-intrusive advertisements supporting free utility features.
- **Privacy Safeguard:** Users can reset or delete their Advertising ID at any time via Android System Settings (*Settings > Google > Ads*).

